error[SCXML003]: identifier `1st state` is not an XML NCName
 --> tests/ui/scxml003-invalid-ncname-references.scx:2:14
  |
1 | <scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml" version="1.0" initial="1st state">
  |                                                                       --------- referenced here
2 |   <state id="1st state"><transition event="go" target="done"/></state>
  |              ^^^^^^^^^ invalid NCName
  |
  = note: SCXML IDs are XML IDs: they must start with a letter or `_` and contain only NCName characters (no spaces or colons), so references can be tokenized unambiguously. An `id` is `xsd:ID`, whose white space collapses (XML Schema 1.1 Part 2 §4.3.6), so leading and trailing white space is not part of it: `id=" s "` declares `s`
  = help: start with a letter or underscore and use only NCName characters; colons are not allowed
  = spec: SCXML 1.0 §3.14 IDs
